The prompt’s index rule is easiest to verify with a self-recursive implementation that removes the last element: the recursive call sees the unchanged prefix indices, while the removed element’s index is `len(lst) - 1`. This gives the prover a genuine induction step over the input list without introducing a task-specific helper oracle.
